# System Information
You are an expert in Java and in analyzing the impact of source code changes on other code entities in a project's production code.

# General Information
You receive information about a set of changes, called seed changes, that were made to fix a bug reported in Jira.
You also receive the Jira bug report title and description and an initial impact set consisting of the fully qualified names of code entities that are statically related to the seed changes.

# Task
Your task is to refine the initial impact set.
A code entity is part of the impact set if it requires modification or, if it does not already exist, must be created as a consequence of the seed changes.
First, remove code entities unless the provided information indicates that they must be modified.
Second, add code entities that must be modified or created according to the provided evidence.

Your goal is to report a final impact set that consists of the fully qualified names of code entities that must be modified or created because of the seed changes.

# Inputs
- Jira bug report title: CPIO fails decoding multibyte name entries
- Jira bug report description: Having a CPIO archive in (e.g. UTF-8) mode and having a name entry with a name containing multi-byte characters the decoder fails.

The problem IMHO is the "getHeaderPadCount" method, which assumes a single byte per character:


{code:java}
 public int getHeaderPadCount(){
 if (this.alignmentBoundary == 0) { return 0; }
 int size = this.headerSize + 1; // Name has terminating null
 if (name != null) {
 size += name.length();
 }
 final int remain = size % this.alignmentBoundary;
 if (remain > 0){
 return this.alignmentBoundary - remain;
 }
 return 0;
 }
{code}
However this may (or may not) be true for UTF-8.



Also it wouldn't be enough to call "String#getBytes(…)" as this might already transform the underlying bytes.

The proper solution would be to provide the name size, as read from the CPIO stream, and pass it to the entry.
- Seed changes and their Git diff hunks: [{"fqn": "org.apache.commons.compress.archivers.cpio.CpioArchiveEntry.getHeaderPadCount(org.apache.commons.compress.archivers.zip.ZipEncoding)", "git_diff_hunk": "@@ -490 +488 @@ public int getHeaderPadCount(){
- public int getHeaderPadCount(ZipEncoding encoding) {
+ public int getHeaderPadCount(Charset charset) {
@@ -494 +492 @@ public int getHeaderPadCount(ZipEncoding encoding) {
- if (encoding == null) {
+ if (charset == null) {
@@ -497,7 +495 @@ public int getHeaderPadCount(ZipEncoding encoding) {
- try {
- final ByteBuffer buf = encoding.encode(name);
- return getHeaderPadCount(buf.limit() - buf.position());
- } catch (IOException ex) {
- // won't happen as the output stream has already encoded the name without error
- throw new RuntimeException("cannot encode " + name, ex);
- }
+ return getHeaderPadCount(name.getBytes(charset).length);"}]
- Initial static code change impact set: ["org.apache.commons.compress.archivers.cpio.CpioArchiveEntry.CpioArchiveEntry(java.io.File,java.lang.String)", "org.apache.commons.compress.archivers.cpio.CpioArchiveEntry.CpioArchiveEntry(java.lang.String)", "org.apache.commons.compress.archivers.cpio.CpioArchiveEntry.CpioArchiveEntry(java.lang.String,long)", "org.apache.commons.compress.archivers.cpio.CpioArchiveEntry.CpioArchiveEntry(short)", "org.apache.commons.compress.archivers.cpio.CpioArchiveEntry.CpioArchiveEntry(short,java.io.File,java.lang.String)", "org.apache.commons.compress.archivers.cpio.CpioArchiveEntry.CpioArchiveEntry(short,java.lang.String)", "org.apache.commons.compress.archivers.cpio.CpioArchiveEntry.CpioArchiveEntry(short,java.lang.String,long)", "org.apache.commons.compress.archivers.cpio.CpioArchiveEntry.alignmentBoundary", "org.apache.commons.compress.archivers.cpio.CpioArchiveEntry.charset", "org.apache.commons.compress.archivers.cpio.CpioArchiveEntry.getHeaderPadCount()", "org.apache.commons.compress.archivers.cpio.CpioArchiveEntry.getHeaderPadCount(long)", "org.apache.commons.compress.archivers.cpio.CpioArchiveEntry.headerSize", "org.apache.commons.compress.archivers.cpio.CpioArchiveEntry.name", "org.apache.commons.compress.archivers.cpio.CpioArchiveEntry.setName(java.lang.String)", "org.apache.commons.compress.archivers.cpio.CpioArchiveOutputStream.writeNewEntry(org.apache.commons.compress.archivers.cpio.CpioArchiveEntry)", "org.apache.commons.compress.archivers.cpio.CpioArchiveOutputStream.writeOldBinaryEntry(org.apache.commons.compress.archivers.cpio.CpioArchiveEntry,boolean)", "org.apache.commons.compress.archivers.zip.ZipEncoding.encode(java.lang.String)"]

# Output Format
Return exactly one valid single-line JSON array of strings.
Each string must be the fully qualified name of an impacted code entity.
Do not include any additional text, formatting, or meta-information.
Do not include seed changes in the output.

Example output (four impacted code entities):
["com.example.Foo.someMethod(java.lang.String, int)", "com.example.bar.attribute1", "com.example.bar.Class.NestedClass", "com.example.bar.Class.Class()"]

Example output (two impacted code entities):
["com.example.package.ParentClass.ChildClass.field", "com.example.package.ParentClass.apply(long, com.example.package.ParentClass)"]

Example output (zero impacted code entities):
[]
